condition_name: Scleritis/Episcleritis
condition_slug: scleritis-episcleritis
source: NSTG 2022
introduction: Inflammation of the sclera and episclera which is usually self-limiting but relapses may occur. It is also usually unilateral and associated with collagen disorders.
clinical_features[1]:
  - type: clinical
    features[2]: "Dull, deep-seated pain in the eye",Localized conjunctival congestion
investigations[1]: Investigate for collagen diseases
treatment:
  goals[0]:
  non_drug[0]:
  drug[2]: Topical steroids or NSAIDs for the duration of symptoms,Treat arthritis if active
  adverse_reactions_and_cautions[1]: Avoid prolonged use of steroids
  supportive_measures[0]:
differential_diagnoses[3]: Pterygium,Phlyctenular conjunctivitis,Trauma to the eye
complications[3]: Thinning of the sclera,Anterior staphyloma,Scleral perforation
prevention[1]: No real preventive measures available
other_investigations: null
definitive_treatment: null
prognosis: null